    {
      "id": 227740,
      "name": "Tubafolk",
      "username": "Tubafolk",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/d07c76/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2019-06-04T13:50:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Thank you Powerhound. Wasn’t sure how to fix that on my end...</p>\n<p>I went combing through Daybreak’s hero sheets and their Reactions have language that answers my question. An example from Rockstar’s abilities:&nbsp;</p>\n<p>“When you change personal zones you may boost by rolling your SINGLE transmutation die.”</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Given that all of Daybreak’s inherent and reaction abilities read as such, notating a single die, I’m going to assume in the Kickstarter heroes it is a single die&nbsp;as well. Most likely the awesome folks here and at GTG have caught that and are making the adjustment.&nbsp;</p>",
      "post_number": 5,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T06:02:00.156Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 1,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.2,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 19233,
      "topic_slug": "question-reactions-and-inherent-rolls",
      "display_username": "Tubafolk",
      "primary_group_name": null,
      "flair_name": null,
      "flair_url": null,
      "flair_bg_color": null,
      "flair_color": null,
      "flair_group_id": null,
      "badges_granted": [],
      "version": 1,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_delete": false,
      "can_recover": false,
      "can_see_hidden_post": false,
      "can_wiki": false,
      "read": false,
      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>Thank you Powerhound. Wasn’t sure how to fix that on my end...</p>\r\n\r\n<p>I went combing through Daybreak’s hero sheets and their Reactions have language that answers my question. An example from Rockstar’s abilities:&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>“When you change personal zones you may boost by rolling your SINGLE transmutation die.”</p>\r\n\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n\r\n<p>Given that all of Daybreak’s inherent and reaction abilities read as such, notating a single die, I’m going to assume in the Kickstarter heroes it is a single die&nbsp;as well. Most likely the awesome folks here and at GTG have caught that and are making the adjustment.&nbsp;</p>",
